course: dictionary
lesson: 1542
title: One word, two jobs: chair
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Many words have more than one meaning. The word chair is a good example. Read the words around it to find out which meaning the writer means. «Never pull a chair away as someone sits; they can fall and badly hurt their back or head.» People sit on this chair, so here it means a seat.
explain: Now read this: «Chairs scraped, everybody jumped up to watch and some even shouted "go on!"» Chairs scraped across the floor, so these are the seats being moved. Ask yourself: what word would fit here, and does my meaning still make sense in the sentence?
explain: Chair can also be a doing word, a verb. To chair a meeting is to lead it. The person who runs the meeting is the chair, or chairperson. When you meet chair in a sentence about a meeting, check whether it means a seat or someone leading.
fact: A chair is a seat for one person, with a back and usually four legs.
fact: The chair, or chairperson, is the person who runs a meeting.
fact: To chair a meeting means to lead it.
fact: Chair can be a noun (chair, chairs) or a verb (chair, chairs, chaired, chairing).
fact: Phrases with chair include armchair, wheelchair, high chair, musical chairs and take a chair.
exercise: «Never pull a chair away as someone sits; they can fall and badly hurt their back or head.» In this sentence, what is a chair? | *A seat for one person | The person who leads a meeting | To lead a meeting | A kind of musical game
exercise: The chair of the school council opened the meeting. Who is the chair? | A long wooden table | A wheelchair for a visitor | *The person who runs the meeting | The seat at the back of the room
exercise: «Ben was asked to chair the meeting.» What does chair mean here? | To sit down quietly | To move the furniture | To write the notes | *To lead the meeting
test: In «Never stand on a chair or climb anything on a balcony», what is a chair? | *A seat | Someone who leads a meeting | A kind of game | A balcony railing
test: Which word in «She will chair the meeting tomorrow» is a verb? | she | tomorrow | meeting | *chair
exam: Which statement about chair is true? | Chair can only be a noun | Chairs are only found in classrooms | Chair means to stand up | *Chair can be a noun, such as a seat, or a verb, such as to lead a meeting
